n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{AB}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/eba964fd799b57b787ab20955b8717b02219ed785d2455cb122e08c448b43563.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $C$ to $\\overset{⟷}{AB}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/adc7bbe174cdc56b7146d85bdec6e568e2cf829a3a64c73f6555e62c168c2eeb.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-27826"] :question/worked-solution "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HCA+m∠ACB & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{125}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA & ={55}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $△AHC$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HCA+m∠HAC+m∠AHC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {55}^{∘}+m∠HAC+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC+{145}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC & ={35}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-27832/selection/8c67eea01d8938bcf5b5511867d2afa0fc68682ba237ff8b210de282b2bc64f4" :answer/id #uuid "d40f489c-1a3e-50f5-8b07-56786d2d0be0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-27832/selection/0fe39b4e66699b1a7eb1c40a28632d17621e5f1ef17a4bafdcd47fac82b383c8" :answer/id #uuid "2743ce8d-86d7-5274-9dd1-b19418d2441a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{18}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-27832/selection/79646158e731768cad156c41b1acc7e7d3c8f0b1c929111f383ed45a4d9840ee" :answer/id #uuid "638b911f-b768-5c73-a1ec-3af084aa24e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{20}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-27832/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78